# Of a list and a number only the list is a cell, so Array.isArray is one mask and one branch: the type byte of the cell is not read and the built-in is not called. The length is read right behind the branch.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="first" role=Source
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[notCell]] = BitAnd(b@[[value]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[notCell]], Terminal
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#[[number]], Else:#[[list]]
# What is no list is a number: the other arm asks nothing more of the word and leaves by no rare edge. It takes the double out of the word, since both arms return a double.
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[number]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #0
# CHECK-NOT: Rare:#
# CHECK: BB#[[list]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors: #0
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[storage]] = Load(b@[[value]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSArray_butterfly
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[storage]], offset = -8, ControlDependent|Reads:Butterfly_publicLength
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# NONE-LABEL: name="first" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: JSCell_typeInfoType
# NONE-NOT: :CallBuiltin)
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# X64-LABEL: name="first" role=Source
# X64-NEXT: instructions: 12, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64-LABEL: name="first" role=Source
# ARM64-NEXT: instructions: 12, patchpoints: 0
